<title>UK: HORSE RACING-SUSSEX STAKES RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-SUSSEX STAKES RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>GOODWOOD, England 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group</p>
<p>one Sussex Stakes for three-year-olds and upwards, run over one</p>
<p>mile (1.6 kms) on Wednesday:</p>
<p>1. Ali-Royal 13-2 (ridden by Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>2. Starborough 9-4 favourite (Pat Eddery)</p>
<p>3. Allied Forces 9-2 (John Reid)</p>
<p>Nine ran</p>
<p>Distances: 3/4 length, same</p>
<p>Winner owned by Greenbay Stables Limited and trained in</p>
<p>England by Henry Cecil.</p>
<p>    Value to winning owner: 92,770 pounds ($151,000)</p>
</text>
